{
 // LSE Project Tools configuration (Lake Shore Electric, AutoCAD Electrical 2026).
 // Point LSEPROJECTSETTINGS at a shared copy on the vault so every engineer creates identical projects.
 //
 // Everything in here was taken from the live LSE standard on 2026-11-10:
 //   - the custom project template  ...\ECAD Standards\Project Templates\CUSTOM TEMPLATES\CUSTOM PROJECT TEMPLATE 2.0\
 //     (E-CAD CUSTOM PROJECT TEMPLATE 2.wdp / .wdt / _wdtitle.wdl / .aepx, DRAWING-#.dwg, STOCKCODE-E001.dwg)
 //   - Locations.txt (the Custom Sales Order folder tree on the vault)
 //   - the workstation's recent-file list (job folders such as 001096-1_AEC Contractors\001096-1.wdp, drawings such as 000924-1-E303.dwg)
 //
 // vault            -> where the LSE standard lives. standardsRoot and jobsRoot are the vault working-folder paths; templateProject is the
 //                     base project every new job copies its +[n] option and ?[n] property lines from; drawingTemplate and coverTemplate
 //                     are file names inside the template folder (DRAWING-#.dwg is the blank LSE sheet, STOCKCODE-E001.dwg the cover).
 // job              -> the LSE job number rule (six-digit sales order, dash, release: 001096-1) and the naming patterns derived from it.
 //                     Tokens: {JOB} {CUSTOMER} {QUOTE} {PROJECT} {USER} {DATE} {YEAR} {SHEET} {SHEET:3}. {CUSTOMER} is description line
 //                     role "customer" made safe for a folder name.
 // descriptionLines -> the *[n] project description lines exactly as the LSE template defines them (labels from _wdtitle.wdl, attributes
 //                     from the .wdt). role: "title" (required, one line), "quote", "customer" (feeds {CUSTOMER}), "designation", "specs"
 //                     (filled by the unit-specs builder), "scale", "date", "user", "job". placeholder is the template's own placeholder text.
 // titleBlock       -> the LSE title block ECAD_LSE_CUSTOM_TB_2.0 and the attributes the template .wdt maps: DWG_NUMBER = FILENAME,
 //                     DWG_TYPE = DD1 (drawing description 1). The LSE block has no SHEET / SHEETMAX mapping, so those are blank.
 // wdm              -> attribute tags on the AutoCAD Electrical WD_M drawing-settings block.
 // unitSpecs        -> choices for the unit-specs builder that composes description line 7 ("SWBD, 2500A, 277/480VAC, 65KA@480V, N1").
 // productLines     -> the Custom Sales Order folder tree (Locations.txt). levels name the cascading choices; children is the tree; a job
 //                     folder is created under the deepest choice made. Every level box is editable, so a new amperage or manufacturer
 //                     can be typed. unitType pre-selects the unit-specs builder; projectType pre-selects the drawing set.
 // projectTypes     -> the drawing sets. fileNamePattern {JOB}-E{SHEET:3} gives 001096-1-E001.dwg. sheet is the E-number of the row
 //                     (optional; rows without one are numbered after the previous row). template is a file name inside the template
 //                     folder or a full path. folder is the Project Manager tree folder (=====SUB=), section/subsection the = / == codes;
 //                     the LSE template uses none of these, so they are left blank.
 //                     The E-number series below (E001 cover, E1xx one-line, E2xx elevations, E3xx schematics, E4xx metering,
 //                     E5xx schedules) is inferred from existing jobs (000924-1-E303.dwg) and must be confirmed against a finished job.
